7/STScI-01KXZZ6H029XBJTKYKRPARFJE9.jpg?w=2000&#038;h=1161&#038;fit=crop&#038;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 8502px) 100vw, 8502px\" /></figure>\n</p></div>\n</p></div>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"grid-col-8 desktop:grid-col-10 padding-left-3 desktop:padding-left-0\">\n<div class=\"grid-row flex-align-center\">\n<div class=\"grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-6\">\n<h2 class=\"heading-36 margin-0\">Andromeda Galaxy</h2>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-6\">\n<p class=\"p-md margin-0 color-carbon-black-important\">NASAâ€™s Hubble Space Telescope has provided a detailed view of millions of stars in the Andromeda galaxy. </p>\n</p></div>\n</p></div>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"grid-col-2 desktop:grid-col-1 display-flex flex-justify-end\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/asset/hubble/andromeda-galaxy/\" target=\"\" aria-label=\"Andromeda Galaxy\" class=\"link-external-false\" rel=\"noopener\"><br />\n                            <svg class=\"hds-featured-link-list-button margin-left-auto margin-right-0\" viewBox=\"0 0 32 32\" fill=\"none\">\n                                <circle class=\"color-nasa-red\" cx=\"16\" cy=\"16\" r=\"16\"></circle><path d=\"M8 16.956h12.604l-3.844 4.106 1.252 1.338L24 16l-5.988-6.4-1.252 1.338 3.844 4.106H8v1.912z\" class=\"color-spacesuit-white\"></path>\n                            </svg><br />\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n</p></div>\n</p></div>\n<div class=\"grid-row padding-y-2 border-top-1px border-color-carbon-30-important\">\n<div class=\"grid-row featured-link-list-row width-full flex-align-center\">\n<div class=\"grid-col-2 desktop:grid-col-1 tablet:padding-right-3 desktop:padding-right-5\">\n<div class=\"width-full\">\n<div class=\"hds-cover-wrapper width-full ratio-1x1 radius-pill overflow-hidden\">\n<figure class=\"hds-media-background  \"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" src=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/missions/hubble/releases/2026/07/STScI-01KY7FCQSFZQV2HS57RRQSQF9N.jpg?w=1280&#038;h=720&#038;fit=clip&#038;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"On a black background, a pixelated, partial ring of bright pink and purple extends from 8 ou2019clock clockwise to 3 ou2019clock. There is a black gap at the bottom of the ring as well as in the middle. Below the ring, a timeline labeled millions of years ago lists the numbers 500, 200, 100, 50, 25, 0. The numbers 500 and 200 are yellow with a yellow line between them, indicating that the image shows the rate of star formation that was occurring in that timeframe.\" style=\"transform: scale(1.2); transform-origin: 50% 50%; object-position: 50% 50%; object-fit: cover;\" block_context=\"nasa-block\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/missions/hubble/releases/2026/07/STScI-01KY7FCQSFZQV2HS57RRQSQF9N.jpg?w=1280&#038;h=720&#038;fit=crop&#038;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1280w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/missions/hubble/releases/2026/07/STScI-01KY7FCQSFZQV2HS57RRQSQF9N.jpg?w=300&#038;h=169&#038;fit=crop&#038;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 300w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/missions/hubble/releases/2026/07/STScI-01KY7FCQSFZQV2HS57RRQSQF9N.jpg?w=768&#038;h=432&#038;fit=crop&#038;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 768w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/missions/hubble/releases/2026/07/STScI-01KY7FCQSFZQV2HS57RRQSQF9N.jpg?w=1024&#038;h=576&#038;fit=crop&#038;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1024w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/missions/hubble/releases/2026/07/STScI-01KY7FCQSFZQV2HS57RRQSQF9N.jpg?w=400&#038;h=225&#038;fit=crop&#038;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 400w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/missions/hubble/releases/2026/07/STScI-01KY7FCQSFZQV2HS57RRQSQF9N.jpg?w=600&#038;h=338&#038;fit=crop&#038;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 600w, https://assets.s