+{
+  "attempt": 1,
+  "raw_response": "{\"headline\": \"NASA Astronaut Chris Williams to Discuss Space Station Mission\", \"dek\": \"NASA astronaut Chris Williams will recap his recent eight-month mission aboard the International Space Station during a news conference on August 4 at 2:45 p.m. EDT from NASAâ€™s Johnson Space Center in Houston. The event will be streamed live through various platforms.\", \"body_markdown\": \"NASA astronaut and Expedition 74 flight engineer Chris Williams will discuss his recent eight-month mission aboard the International Space Station during a news conference at 2:45 p.m. EDT on Tuesday, August 4, from NASAâ€™s Johnson Space Center in Houston. The event will be streamed live through various platforms, and details on how to watch online are available at [https://www.nasa.gov/live](https://www.nasa.gov/live). \\n\\nWilliams returned to Earth on July 26, after logging 241 days as an Expedition 73/74 flight engineer during his first spaceflight. He returned along with Roscosmos cosmonauts Sergey Kud-Sverchkov and Sergei Mikaev, completing 3,856 orbits of the Earth over the course of their more than 102-million-mile journey. They also witnessed the arrival of six visiting spacecraft and the departure of eight. \\n\\nDuring his mission, Williams supported a wide range of scientific investigations and technology demonstrations. He helped advance research for new cancer treatments and improved in-space manufacturing of materials used in high-performance computers and electronics. Williams also completed two spacewalks to prepare for space station power system upgrades and to replace a faulty joint on the Canadarm2 robotic arm. \\n\\nThe crewâ€™s work aboard the space station helps improve life on Earth and prepare for future human missions to the Moon and Mars. To learn more about International Space Station research, operations, and its crews, visit [http://www.nasa.gov/station](http://www.nasa.gov/station). \\n\\nFor media interested in attending the event in person, contact the NASA Johnson newsroom no later than 5 p.m., Friday, July 31, at jsccommu@mail.nasa.gov. Media wishing to participate by phone must contact the Johnson newsroom no later than two hours before the start of the event. To ask a question by phone, media must dial into the news conference no later than 15 minutes prior to the start of the call. \\n\\nNASAâ€™s media accreditation policy is available online. \\n\\nFor more information, contact: \\n\\nJoshua Finch \\nHeadquarters, Washington \\n202-358-1100 \\njoshua.a.finch@nasa.gov \\n\\nAnna Schneider \\nJohnson Space Center, Houston \\n281-483-5111 \\nanna.c.schneider@nasa.gov\", \"claim_to_source\": [{\"claim\": \"NASA Astronaut Chris Williams will discuss his eight-month mission aboard the International Space Station\", \"source_ids\": [\"source:32b0ce89958dc3e3c7392e11418cc059e31eab4698e89c6aa95f931824f29a5c:9d6d7312-473d-4119-a64d-4ea4c53b8603:1\"]}, {\"claim\": \"The event will take place on August 4 at 2:45 p.m. EDT\", \"source_ids\": [\"source:32b0ce89958dc3e3c7392e11418cc059e31eab4698e89c6aa95f931824f29a5c:9d6d7312-473d-4119-a64d-4ea4c53b8603:1\"]}, {\"claim\": \"The news conference will be held at NASAâ€™s Johnson Space Center in Houston\", \"source_ids\": [\"source:32b0ce89958dc3e3c7392e11418cc059e31eab4698e89c6aa95f931824f29a5c:9d6d7312-473d-4119-a64d-4ea4c53b8603:1\"]}, {\"claim\": \"NASA will stream the event live through various platforms\", \"source_ids\": [\"source:32b0ce89958dc3e3c7392e11418cc059e31eab4698e89c6aa95f931824f29a5c:9d6d7312-473d-4119-a64d-4ea4c53b8603:1\"]}]}",
